    <summary>IPMICFG is an in-band utility for configuring IPMI devices. It is a command line tool providing standard IPMI and Supermicro® proprietary OEM commands.</summary>
    <description>IPMICFG is an in-band utility for configuring IPMI devices. It is a command line tool providing standard IPMI and Supermicro® proprietary OEM commands. This CLI-based utility can be executed on DOS, Windows, and Linux OS and does not require any installation procedures. This utility is used for BMC/FRU configuration.

IPMICFG Key Features:

  - Set up IPMI IP Address
  - Set up IPMI Configuration
  - Configure IPMI User Management
  - Configure IPMI FRU
  - Manage System Event Log (SEL)
  - Manage IPMI by node management (NM) protocol</description>
    <releaseNotes>## IPMICFG 1.35.2 (build 240627)

Released 2024-06-27 (build date).
- Embeds the official archive from Supermicro's download center
  (`https://www.supermicro.com/Bios/sw_download/760/IPMICFG_1.35.2_build.240627.zip`), redistributed with Supermicro's permission — nothing is downloaded at install time;
  see legal\VERIFICATION.txt.
- sha256 `5CB3DAD030680772AC6160F9826F3BAABA10ABA2072CB9D5EC8E4A4DB94E81DA`.
- Extracts only the matching-bitness `Windows\<32|64>bit` folder; the command is `ipmicfg`.
    </releaseNotes>
